CONTRACT DEFINITION:
1. RESEARCH NOTE: See plan/010_8645157f3bf5/bugfix/001_07ad0d602ba9/architecture/source_analysis.md (§1-2, §6) and fix_strategy.md (BUG-001 section). URL_SHAPE_RE is defined at file-injector.ts:36 and has exactly ONE runtime consumer — URL_SHAPE_RE.test(tok) at L1398 inside the URL scan loop (L1395-1402). The scheme-less dotted-host alternative B matches ANY <word>.<2+alpha-letters> token, so code-file extensions (go, md, py, json, etc.) pass the gate as fake alpha-TLDs.
2. INPUT: The URL scan loop at L1395-1402 receives `tok` (the cleanToken'd candidate from URL_INJECT_RE group 2). After URL_SHAPE_RE.test(tok) passes at L1398, the token is normalized to absolute form at L1399 (scheme-less tokens get 'https://' prepended). The current loop body is:
   if (enableUrls) {
     for (const m of text.matchAll(URL_INJECT_RE)) {
       const tok = cleanToken(m[2]);
       if (tok && URL_SHAPE_RE.test(tok)) {
         const abs = /^https?:\/\//i.test(tok) ? tok : "https://" + tok;
         if (!state.injectedSet.has(abs)) {
           state.injectedSet.add(abs);
           await injectUrl(abs, state, ctx);
         }
       }
     }
   }
3. LOGIC: (a) Define a new module-level const CODE_EXTENSIONS as a Set<string> containing common code/file extensions (lowercase, no dot). Include at minimum these categories per fix_strategy.md: programming languages (ts, tsx, js, jsx, mjs, cjs, py, rb, go, rs, java, kt, cs, cpp, cc, c, h, hpp, swift, php, pl, lua, r, scala, clj, ex, erl, hs, ml, fs, vb, dart, groovy, el, scm, rkt, zig, nim, jl, d, f, f90, pas, asm, v), web/markup (html, htm, css, scss, sass, less, styl, vue, svelte), config/data (xml, json, json5, jsonc, yaml, yml, toml, ini, cfg, conf, env, sql, graphql, gql, proto, csv, tsv, properties, gradle, cmake), scripts (sh, bash, zsh, fish, ps1, bat, cmd, awk), images (png, jpg, jpeg, gif, webp, bmp, svg, ico, tiff, tif, heic, avif), documents (md, markdown, txt, pdf, doc, docx, xls, xlsx, ppt, pptx, rtf, tex, bib, rst, adoc), binary/archives (db, sqlite, zip, tar, gz, bz2, xz, 7z, rar, lock, log, min, map, wasm). Place it near URL_SHAPE_RE (around L37). (b) Add a post-gate check inside the URL scan loop: AFTER URL_SHAPE_RE.test(tok) passes AND the token is identified as scheme-less (i.e., !/^https?:\/\//i.test(tok) AND !/^ftp:\/\//i.test(tok)), extract the final label — the substring after the LAST '.' in tok, lowercased — and check CODE_EXTENSIONS.has(finalLabel). If it IS a code extension, skip this token (continue the loop — no fetch, no normalization, no injection). Explicit-scheme tokens (https://, http://, ftp://) must NEVER be checked against the deny-list — they bypass it entirely. (c) Write the failing test FIRST: add a test case in url-injection.test.mjs that asserts calls.length===0 for 'edit #main.go' (TDD). Then implement the gate. Then verify the test passes. (d) Update the JSDoc comment block above URL_SHAPE_RE (L27-35) to document the CODE_EXTENSIONS deny-list gate and remove the false claim that '#node.js' is 'the only residual false-positive class' and that it is 'benign.' State clearly that scheme-less tokens whose final label is a known code extension are treated as file references, not URLs. Document that explicit-scheme tokens bypass the deny-list.
4. OUTPUT: The modified file-injector.ts with: (a) the CODE_EXTENSIONS Set constant near L37, (b) the post-gate check in the URL scan loop at ~L1398-1400, (c) updated JSDoc. No new exports needed — CODE_EXTENSIONS is private/module-level. The injectFiles return shape is UNCHANGED. The behavior change: scheme-less tokens with code-extension final labels no longer trigger fetches.
